  "allow_request_redirects": false,
  "enforce_tls_upstream": false,
  "gateway_may_retry_non_idempotent": false,
  "notes": "Example for the WanbExpress sandbox. TENANT-ID-*, CLIENT-ID-* are placeholders: fill in the Gatekeeper tenant ids and the M2M client ids (the sub of the caller's token) when deploying. account-blue and account-green are the ids of the provider_account objects in Gatekeeper and the second part of the developer-token file's handles (gatekeeper:wanbexpress-test/account-blue). enforce_tls_upstream is false because the sandbox is plain HTTP; gateway-authz does not read the field (it ignores everything outside the rows' decision fields). A production upstream must be https."
